<?php
/**
 * Copyright © ElAssal for Trading & Supply. All rights reserved.
 *
 * Language switcher — Figma node 595:14481 (globe + store name + chevron).
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHY THIS OVERRIDE EXISTS
 * ===========================================================================
 * Porto's copy of this template opens the panel with
 *
 *     data-mage-init='{"dropdownDialog": ... }'
 *
 * and `dropdownDialog` is `mage/dropdown`, whose first dependency is
 * `jquery-ui-modules/dialog`. Measured on the live Arabic checkout
 * (Lighthouse, 2026-09-05, incognito) that one attribute pulled TEN modules,
 * 25,915 transferred bytes and 97,819 parsed bytes of draggable/resizable
 * modal-dialog machinery — to show a list of two store views. The two flag
 * PNGs it also requested (`wysiwyg/smartwave/porto/flags/ar.png`, `en.png`,
 * parser-discovered at 1,143 ms) are proof it renders on checkout, where
 * Spartrak has otherwise already stripped the header down.
 *
 * `<details>`/`<summary>` is the HTML element for a disclosure. It carries the
 * open/close state, the click and Enter/Space handling, the focusability and
 * the implicit `aria-expanded` itself, in every browser since 2020, and it
 * still works with JavaScript off. Only LIGHT DISMISS — close on outside click
 * or Escape, which `dropdownDialog` did by default — needs script, and
 * web/js/spartrak-disclosure.js is ~30 lines of dependency-free DOM for it.
 *
 * This is also an accessibility fix. Porto's trigger is a bare
 * `<div class="action toggle">` with no tabindex and no role: the control
 * could not be reached or operated from the keyboard at all. `<summary>` is
 * natively focusable and operable (CLAUDE.md section 15).
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CARRIED OVER
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE FLAGS. Porto renders a flag <img> beside the store name in the trigger
 * and beside every option, gated on `porto_settings/header/language_flag`.
 * Figma's control is globe + store name + chevron, with no flag, and
 * components/_support-strip.less already hid them with `.switcher img
 * { display: none }`. Hidden is not free: both PNGs were still downloaded on
 * every page. They are not emitted at all now. That LESS rule is kept as a
 * safety net for any other switcher template Porto may render.
 *
 * THE `$is_demo` BRANCH. Porto ships a hardcoded `$is_demo = 0` and a dead
 * "Add More" French option behind it. Dead code, dropped.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHY `data-post` AND NOT CORE'S `getViewModel()`
 * ===========================================================================
 * Magento 2.4.8's own copy of this template builds a plain `<a href>` from
 * `$block->getViewModel()->getTargetStoreRedirectUrl($_lang)`. That is the
 * better markup — but the block instance this template renders for is
 * declared in Spartrak's Smartwave_Porto/layout/default.xml with NO view model
 * argument, and calling getViewModel() on it fatals with "Call to a member
 * function getTargetStoreRedirectUrl() on null" on every page. That exact
 * failure was shipped and reverted on 2026-08-24; see the note at the head of
 * components/_support-strip.less. The POST payload is what this block instance
 * supports, so the POST payload is what stays.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Store\Block\Switcher $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 */
?>
<?php if (count($block->getStores()) > 1) : ?>
    <?php $id = $block->getIdModifier() ? '-' . $block->getIdModifier() : ''; ?>
    <div class="switcher language switcher-language"
         data-ui-id="language-switcher"
         id="switcher-language<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($id) ?>">
        <strong class="label switcher-label"><span><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Language')) ?></span></strong>
        <?php /*
          The classes are Porto's and Magento's, unchanged, because
          components/_support-strip.less and Porto's own stylesheet both hang
          off them. Only the ELEMENT changes: <div> to <details>, and the
          trigger <div> to <summary>.
        */ ?>
        <details class="actions dropdown options switcher-options"
                 data-mage-init='{"spartrakDisclosure":{}}'>
            <summary class="action toggle switcher-trigger"
                     id="switcher-language-trigger<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($id) ?>">
                <strong class="view-<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($block->getCurrentStoreCode()) ?>">
                    <span><?= $block->escapeHtml($block->getStoreName()) ?></span>
                </strong>
            </summary>
            <ul class="dropdown switcher-dropdown">
                <?php foreach ($block->getStores() as $_lang) : ?>
                    <?php if ($_lang->getId() != $block->getCurrentStoreId()) : ?>
                        <li class="view-<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr($_lang->getCode()) ?> switcher-option">
                            <?php /*
                              @noEscape: getTargetStorePostData() returns a
                              JSON payload the block itself builds and encodes,
                              and mage/dataPost reads it back with
                              JSON.parse(). Escaping it here is what Magento
                              core does not do either, in this same template.
                            */ ?>
                            <a href="#" data-post='<?= /* @noEscape */ $block->getTargetStorePostData($_lang) ?>'>
                                <?= $block->escapeHtml($_lang->getName()) ?>
                            </a>
                        </li>
                    <?php endif; ?>
                <?php endforeach; ?>
            </ul>
        </details>
    </div>
<?php endif; ?>
